212	## Asynchronous function calling
213	
214	Function calling executes sequentially by default, meaning execution pauses
215	until the results of each function call are available. This ensures sequential
216	processing, which means you won't be able to continue interacting with the model
217	while the functions are being run.
218	
219	> [!NOTE]
220	> **Note:** Asynchronous function calling is not yet supported in Gemini 3.1 Flash Live. The model will not start responding until you've sent the tool response.
221	
222	If you don't want to block the conversation, you can tell the model to run the
223	functions asynchronously. To do so, you first need to add a `behavior` to the
224	function definitions:
225	
226	### Python
227	
228	    # Non-blocking function definitions
229	    turn_on_the_lights = {"name": "turn_on_the_lights", "behavior": "NON_BLOCKING"} # turn_on_the_lights will run asynchronously
230	    turn_off_the_lights = {"name": "turn_off_the_lights"} # turn_off_the_lights will still pause all interactions with the model
231	
232	### JavaScript
233	
234	    import { GoogleGenAI, Modality, Behavior } from '@google/genai';
235	
236	    // Non-blocking function definitions
237	    const turn_on_the_lights = {name: "turn_on_the_lights", behavior: Behavior.NON_BLOCKING}
238	
239	    // Blocking function definitions
240	    const turn_off_the_lights = {name: "turn_off_the_lights"}
241	
242	    const tools = [{ functionDeclarations: [turn_on_the_lights, turn_off_the_lights] }]
243	
244	`NON-BLOCKING` ensures the function runs asynchronously while you can
245	continue interacting with the model.
246	
247	Then you need to tell the model how to behave when it receives the
248	`FunctionResponse` using the `scheduling` parameter. It can either:
249	
250	- Interrupt what it's doing and tell you about the response it got right away (`scheduling="INTERRUPT"`),
251	- Wait until it's finished with what it's currently doing (`scheduling="WHEN_IDLE"`),
252	- Or do nothing and use that knowledge later on in the discussion
253	  (`scheduling="SILENT"`)
254	
255	### Python
256	
257	    # for a non-blocking function definition, apply scheduling in the function response:
258	      function_response = types.FunctionResponse(
259	          id=fc.id,
260	          name=fc.name,
261	          response={
262	              "result": "ok",
263	              "scheduling": "INTERRUPT" # Can also be WHEN_IDLE or SILENT
264	          }
265	      )
266	
267	### JavaScript
268	
269	    import { GoogleGenAI, Modality, Behavior, FunctionResponseScheduling } from '@google/genai';
270	
271	    // for a non-blocking function definition, apply scheduling in the function response:
272	    const functionResponse = {
273	      id: fc.id,
274	      name: fc.name,
275	      response: {
276	        result: "ok",
277	        scheduling: FunctionResponseScheduling.INTERRUPT  // Can also be WHEN_IDLE or SILENT
278	      }
279	    }
